<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<phpunit xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="vendor/phpunit/phpunit/phpunit.xsd"
         bootstrap="tests/bootstrap.php"
         colors="true"
>
    <!--
        Punches that reach the server in the same instant, from separate PHP
        processes, against MySQL/MariaDB.

            ./scripts/gates.sh concurrency

        ## Why this file exists

        Every "duplicate" test in tests/Feature is one process sending two
        punches one after the other. That proves the rule and says nothing
        about a race: the engine's per-person lock and its transaction only
        matter when two requests are in flight together. This suite starts
        real processes, holds them at a barrier and releases them together.

        ## Why it cannot live in the other suites

        - SQLite :memory: is private to one process, so a child sees nothing.
        - RefreshDatabase wraps each test in a transaction, so fixtures are
          never committed and a child sees nothing.
        - CACHE_STORE=array is private to one process, so the engine's lock
          would serialise nobody. Production's store is `database`, and that
          is what is forced here.

        So tests/Concurrency sits outside the Unit and Feature testsuites, as
        tests/Performance does, its fixtures are committed, and it never joins
        the full sweep.

        ## Setup

            CREATE DATABASE ethr_concurrency CHARACTER SET utf8mb4
                COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;

        The suite migrates the database on its first test and leaves its rows
        behind, each run under a tenant of its own. Point it at a scratch
        database only: it refuses a name that does not say `concurrency`,
        `scratch` or `suite`.

        The five settings that locate the server are not forced, as in
        phpunit.mysql.xml, so the environment wins.
    -->
    <testsuites>
        <testsuite name="Concurrency">
            <directory>tests/Concurrency</directory>
        </testsuite>
    </testsuites>
    <php>
        <ini name="memory_limit" value="2G"/>
        <env name="APP_ENV" value="testing" force="true"/>
        <env name="APP_MAINTENANCE_DRIVER" value="file" force="true"/>
        <env name="BCRYPT_ROUNDS" value="4" force="true"/>
        <env name="BROADCAST_CONNECTION" value="null" force="true"/>
        <env name="FRONTEND_URL" value="" force="true"/>
        <env name="CACHE_STORE" value="database" force="true"/>
        <env name="SIGNALS_CACHE_DRIVER" value="array" force="true"/>

        <env name="DB_CONNECTION" value="mysql" force="true"/>
        <env name="DB_HOST" value="127.0.0.1"/>
        <env name="DB_PORT" value="3306"/>
        <env name="DB_DATABASE" value="ethr_concurrency"/>
        <env name="DB_USERNAME" value="root"/>
        <env name="DB_PASSWORD" value=""/>
        <env name="DB_URL" value="" force="true"/>

        <env name="FILESYSTEM_DISK" value="local" force="true"/>
        <env name="MAIL_MAILER" value="array" force="true"/>
        <env name="QUEUE_CONNECTION" value="sync" force="true"/>
        <env name="SESSION_DRIVER" value="array" force="true"/>
    </php>
</phpunit>
